00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.437
Oh, no, you're bleeding.

00:14:16.472 --> 00:14:19.624
Oh, you're bleeding!

00:14:20.542 --> 00:14:22.776
I'll just go clean up. It's nothing.

00:14:22.811 --> 00:14:24.244
No, no, no, wait. I have tissues.

00:14:24.279 --> 00:14:26.045
Lots and lots of tissues.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:29.515
My friend Victoria buys them in bulk.

00:14:30.854 --> 00:14:32.713
There. That should be enough.

00:14:32.748 --> 00:14:34.947
I mean, that's better.

00:14:35.994 --> 00:14:38.751
You know, I'd really prefer
white wine if you have it.

00:14:39.191 --> 00:14:40.690
Oh, okay.

00:14:40.725 --> 00:14:42.813
Coming right up.

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:48.363
Any particular kind of--

00:14:48.398 --> 00:14:50.665
What are you doing?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.301
Oh, nothing. It's just a baggie.

00:14:53.336 --> 00:14:56.670
My friend Victoria gets
those by the bulk too.

00:14:56.705 --> 00:15:00.006
She's nuts, that woman...

00:15:00.041 --> 00:15:02.876
Crazy, crazy, crazy Victoria.

00:15:06.262 --> 00:15:08.571
Why are you collecting my blood?

00:15:08.606 --> 00:15:10.607
Oh, well, you know,

00:15:10.782 --> 00:15:13.441
Collecting blood is all the rage now.

00:15:13.476 --> 00:15:17.265
<i>True blood, Twilight, New Moon, Eclipse.</i>

00:15:17.427 --> 00:15:18.522
I get it.

00:15:20.062 --> 00:15:22.393
So, what are you... a vampire?

00:15:22.427 --> 00:15:25.123
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:15:25.204 --> 00:15:26.886
I don't want to suck your blood.

00:15:26.947 --> 00:15:30.790
I just want to take it home with me.

00:15:35.661 --> 00:15:39.663
I was collecting your DNA, because...

00:15:39.698 --> 00:15:42.165
I think I might possibly be your mother.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.548
My mother?

00:15:43.583 --> 00:15:45.433
It's better that a vampire,

00:15:47.387 --> 00:15:49.971
No, it isn't.

00:15:50.574 --> 00:15:52.760
Look, I-I gave up a baby for adoption.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:54.809
I know my birth mother.

00:15:54.844 --> 00:15:55.910
You do?

00:15:55.945 --> 00:15:58.846
Yeah, I registered on a website.
I met her, like, ten years ago.

00:16:05.075 --> 00:16:08.344
Well, that's fantastic news.

00:16:08.379 --> 00:16:10.540
I'm not your mother.

00:16:10.581 --> 00:16:13.025
We can go back to how we were now.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:16.295
- Um...
- I'll just let myself out.

00:16:18.969 --> 00:16:22.566
Here's to the prettiest
girl in the place.

00:16:22.601 --> 00:16:24.835
Well, thank you.

00:16:34.738 --> 00:16:38.312
- What?
- It's refreshing!

00:16:38.347 --> 00:16:40.314
It's refreshing, isn't it?

00:16:41.278 --> 00:16:42.596
Yeah.

00:16:43.919 --> 00:16:46.520
Plenty more where that came from.

00:16:53.137 --> 00:16:54.926
Hey, what are you doing home so early?

00:16:55.297 --> 00:16:56.728
Did you get the hair?

00:16:57.165 --> 00:16:58.847
He's not my son...

00:16:58.908 --> 00:17:00.469
Or my boyfriend.

00:17:00.489 --> 00:17:03.196
Oh, sweetie, I'm sorry.

00:17:03.231 --> 00:17:04.602
What a night.

00:17:04.637 --> 00:17:05.926
Yeah, I'll say.

00:17:06.068 --> 00:17:07.811
I was out with a handsy 85-year-old

00:17:07.872 --> 00:17:12.143
Who doesn't get "no means no"
because he couldn't hear it.

00:17:16.086 --> 00:17:17.546
Where is Victoria?

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:20.717
Big n easy-- where else?

00:17:20.752 --> 00:17:23.620
She's really getting
addicted to that place.

00:17:23.655 --> 00:17:25.555
- Time for an intervention?
- Yeah, I think so.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:28.023
How many interventions
have we done for her?

00:17:28.058 --> 00:17:30.240
Oh, counting kabbalah and colonics?

00:17:35.064 --> 00:17:37.330
Ooh, look, a crowd-- it
must be something good.

00:17:37.365 --> 00:17:39.398
Ooh, hope there's more
of that beer-battered...

00:17:39.433 --> 00:17:40.733
- What was that?
- Who cares?

00:17:40.768 --> 00:17:42.768
It was battered in beer.

00:17:42.803 --> 00:17:46.570
Don't worry. No detergent
box will go unsigned.

00:17:46.605 --> 00:17:47.705
Victoria?

00:17:48.548 --> 00:17:50.778
Joy. Uh, Melanie.

00:17:50.859 --> 00:17:52.785
What a surprise.

00:17:52.805 --> 00:17:56.012
Would you excuse me for just a moment?

00:18:01.652 --> 00:18:03.670
Darling, isn't this
all a little pathetic?

00:18:03.705 --> 00:18:06.175
Well, some people might think so.

00:18:06.195 --> 00:18:09.460
By the way, how was your
date with your son?

00:18:11.229 --> 00:18:12.763
Turns out he's not my son.

00:18:12.798 --> 00:18:14.597
- Boyfriend?
- Nope.

00:18:14.979 --> 00:18:16.459
- You okay?
- Yep.

00:18:16.925 --> 00:18:19.299
Free samples are helping.

00:18:20.094 --> 00:18:22.797
So you bought all that stuff Just
as an excuse to come down here?

00:18:23.616 --> 00:18:24.528
Yes.

00:18:24.893 --> 00:18:27.427
See, I've been feeling very insecure

00:18:27.487 --> 00:18:29.769
Ever since the edge of
tomorrow was canceled,

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.504
And I-I just didn't want
to burden you two with it.

00:18:32.539 --> 00:18:34.573
You talk about it all the time.

00:18:34.608 --> 00:18:38.209
Yes, but I've really wanted
to talk about it more.

00:18:38.666 --> 00:18:40.711
<i>Attention, big n easy shoppers...</i>

00:18:40.746 --> 00:18:43.446
Can you believe that's us?

00:18:43.481 --> 00:18:45.414
<i>In the deli department,
we are proud to announce</i>

00:18:45.449 --> 00:18:47.416
<i>Our latest yard-long hero sandwich,</i>

00:18:47.451 --> 00:18:48.884
<i>The Victoria Chase.</i>

00:18:48.919 --> 00:18:50.687
You see, I'm a hero.

00:18:50.722 --> 00:18:54.025
Oh, come on. I promised I'd spray on
The first foot of cheese.

00:18:58.174 --> 00:19:00.171
Hey, what are you doing?

00:19:00.206 --> 00:19:03.307
- You won't approve.
- Tell us.

00:19:04.443 --> 00:19:05.909
Googling the ex.

00:19:06.481 --> 00:19:10.546
I found a picture of
Anders and Kim in Paris.

00:19:10.752 --> 00:19:13.517
Apparently, they were flying
to some competition...

00:19:13.552 --> 00:19:16.253
'cause she's a fitness model.

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:21.526
All right, take it from someone who
went searching for validation in bulk.

00:19:24.823 --> 00:19:27.823
Sometimes is just best to let things go.

00:19:28.001 --> 00:19:30.734
Yeah, you're right. What's past is past.

00:19:31.241 --> 00:19:34.545
Still, you can't pretend
it never existed.

00:19:34.585 --> 00:19:37.221
Here, let me have that.

00:19:38.072 --> 00:19:39.776
Tyler mentioned this website

00:19:39.811 --> 00:19:42.579
He used to let his mother
know he was looking for her.

00:19:42.614 --> 00:19:47.517
Oh, joy, this is amazing. Are you
really thinking of finding your son?

00:19:47.552 --> 00:19:49.052
Maybe.

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:51.119
It's all just a...

00:19:51.436 --> 00:19:52.571
A lot.

00:19:52.692 --> 00:19:54.497
I can't imagine.

00:19:54.623 --> 00:19:57.290
Yes, you can. You're a mother.

00:19:57.325 --> 00:20:00.533
Hey, so are you.

00:20:00.614 --> 00:20:02.763
Thanks.

00:20:02.798 --> 00:20:06.066
Oh, it's just so weird to
think of him out there--

00:20:06.101 --> 00:20:08.001
A grown man.

00:20:08.036 --> 00:20:10.903
He could be married,
have kids of his own.

00:20:10.938 --> 00:20:12.738
I might even have...

00:20:12.773 --> 00:20:14.489
Grandkids.

00:20:15.604 --> 00:20:19.243
Hey, maybe one of 'em's old
enough for you to date.

00:20:24.727 --> 00:20:25.883
Too soon?

00:20:25.884 --> 00:20:29.884
